    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dwolta4",
      "content": "Engineering drawings use standardized lines, symbols, and views to represent objects clearly and accurately. These elements help engineers, technicians, and workers understand the shape, size, features, and assembly of machine parts. In technical trades such as fitting, machining, and mechanical maintenance, correct interpretation of drawing lines and symbols is essential."
    },
    {
      "id": "nwnugqk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Importance of Lines and Symbols in Engineering Drawing"
    },
    {
      "id": "j35e36g",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Represent different features of objects",
        "Help identify visible and hidden parts",
        "Provide accurate dimensions and instructions",
        "Ensure clear communication between engineers and workers",
        "Reduce manufacturing errors"
      ]
    },
    {
