    {
      "id": "74vrhgm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Isometric View"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vcmm2kr",
      "content": "Isometric drawing is a pictorial method of representing three-dimensional objects on a two-dimensional surface. In isometric view, the three principal axes are equally inclined at 120°."
    },
    {
      "id": "zedc02p",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Sectional Views"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vcfbg4v",
      "content": "Sectional views are used to show internal features of objects by imagining the object cut by a cutting plane."
    },
